<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1948</h1><p class="ref-lede">1948 in world history: 32 events, 14 births, 19 deaths, 4 works, 12 states founded and 24 that came to an end. 679 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947">1947</a><a href="/years/1948" aria-current="page">1948</a><a href="/years/1949">1949</a><a href="/years/1950">1950</a><a href="/years/1951">1951</a><a href="/years/1952">1952</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Burma becomes independent from Britain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> left British rule as an independent republic outside the Commonwealth, at an hour chosen by astrologers. Independence hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san">Aung San</a> had been assassinated six months earlier, and civil conflict soon followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-30">30 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mahatma Gandhi is assassinated in New Delhi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nationalist Nathuram Godse shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> at a prayer meeting at Birla House. The death of the leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s non-violent independence struggle was mourned across the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-4">4 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ceylon becomes independent from Britain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> became a self-governing dominion in the Commonwealth, ending about 150 years of British rule. It became a republic and took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in 1972.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-17">17 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Brussels Treaty creates a Western European defence pact</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg agreed to defend one another against attack. The pact paved the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 1949 and later became the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-14">14 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">David Ben-Gurion proclaims the State of Israel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As the British Mandate ended, Ben-Gurion declared Israel's independence in Tel Aviv. Neighbouring Arab states invaded the next day, and hundreds of thousands of Palestinians were displaced in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-24">24 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins the Berlin Blockade</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces cut road, rail and canal links to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-berlin">West Berlin</a>. The Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> responded with an airlift that supplied the city's two million people for eleven months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-5">5 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The National Health Service launches in Britain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Aneurin Bevan's National Health Service began, offering comprehensive care free at the point of use to everyone in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. It became one of the defining institutions of the post-war welfare state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-9">9 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">North Korea is proclaimed under Kim Il-sung</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">Democratic People's Republic of Korea</a> was proclaimed in the Soviet-occupied north, weeks after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">Republic of Korea</a> in the south. Kim Il-sung founded a dynasty that still rules.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-10">10 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The UN adopts the Universal Declaration of Human Rights</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the UN General Assembly adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-declaration-of-human-rights">Universal Declaration of Human Rights</a> without a vote against. The drafting committee was chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/operation-polo" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-polo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-polo">Operation Polo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Polo was the Indian military operation of 13-18 September 1948 that ended the independence of Hyderabad State, whose Nizam had refused to join India.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/madiun-affair" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madiun-affair.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/madiun-affair">Madiun Affair</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Madiun Affair was a communist uprising in September 1948 centred on the town of Madiun in East Java, during Indonesia's war of independence against the Netherlands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/finno-soviet-treaty-of-1948" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/finno-soviet-treaty-of-1948.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/finno-soviet-treaty-of-1948">Finno-Soviet Treaty of 1948</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Finno-Soviet Treaty of 1948, formally the Agreement of Friendship, Cooperation and Mutual Assistance, was signed in Moscow on 6 April 1948.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/liaoshen-campaign" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liaoshen-campaign.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/liaoshen-campaign">Liaoshen campaign</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Liaoshen campaign was the first of the three great campaigns of the Chinese Civil War, fought in Manchuria from September to November 1948.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/suket-satyagraha">Suket Satyagraha</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Suket Satyagraha was a popular movement in the princely state of Suket, in the hills of present-day Himachal Pradesh, in February 1948.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/nakba">Nakba</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Nakba, Arabic for catastrophe, is the Palestinian name for the flight and expulsion of roughly 700,000 Palestinian Arabs from their homes during the war surrounding Israel's creation in 1948, and for the destruction of hundreds of their villages.</p></div></li></ol></section>
